 # Changelog
+
+## 0.5.20 - 2026-10-23 (local test candidate; unpublished)
+
+- Ask before starting each online or downloaded video. Offer playback from
+  the beginning or the saved position for the exact film/episode. Without a
+  valid bookmark, offer beginning and cancel; live sources explicitly offer
+  live playback. Keep the existing bookmark validity and completion policy.
+- Apply the same choice to next-episode playback, including complete local
+  downloads, and to streams redirected to an existing downloaded copy.
+- Start no player or online resolver while the choice is pending. Preserve
+  the bookmark on cancellation, invalidate stale account/title/episode
+  choices, and consume a single-selection callback only once.
+- Preserve verified-prefix checks for incomplete downloads. If the prefix
+  becomes insufficient after Resume was offered, report it and require a new
+  choice instead of silently starting from the beginning.
+
+- Use rectangle textures for sampled video planes, selecting the pinned PS5
+  driver's linear upload path instead of CPU tiling for every R8/RG8 frame.
+  Keep the source-sized 2D output and allocation/FBO/lifetime protections.
+- Add a bounded H.264 level-51 retry only after a rejected native memory query
+  and only for a declared compatible profile/level and known1080p coded size.
+  Retain software selection if the native decoder still refuses the stream.
+- Record separate CPU allocation, plane-transfer and conversion-submission
+  times; preserve numeric histograms in runtime.json. Report declared source
+  frame rate separately from accepted-frame cadence. New PS5 measurements
+  remain required to establish the performance improvement.
+
+Title ID: `PPSA74126`. Native content version: `00.070.000`.
+See [local validation and scope](docs/LOCAL_0_5_20_VALIDATION.md).
+Native memory and audio lifetime protections, decoder reference-frame safety
+and L2/R2 controls are retained. No publication or store submission is included.
 
